{
  "id": "JAS.4",
  "number": "4",
  "bookId": "JAS",
  "reference": "James 4",
  "verseCount": 17,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "4",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "JAS 4"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "4",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JAS 4:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "What causes wars, and what causes fightings among you? Is it not your passions that are at war in your members? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JAS.4.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JAS.4.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JAS 4:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "You desire and do not have; so you kill. And you covet",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JAS.4.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JAS.4.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4.2",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Or",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "you kill and you covet",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " and cannot obtain; so you fight and wage war. You do not have, because you do not ask. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JAS.4.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JAS.4.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JAS 4:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "You ask and do not receive, because you ask wrongly, to spend it on your passions. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JAS.4.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JAS.4.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JAS 4:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Unfaithful creatures! Do you not know that friendship with the world is enmity with God? Therefore whoever wishes to be a friend of the world makes himself an enemy of God. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JAS.4.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JAS.4.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JAS 4:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Or do you suppose it is in vain that the scripture says, “He yearns jealously over the spirit which he has made to dwell in us”? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JAS.4.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JAS.4.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JAS 4:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "PRO.3.34"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Prov 3.34",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " But he gives more grace; therefore it says, “God opposes the proud, but gives grace to the humble.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JAS.4.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JAS.4.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JAS 4:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Submit yourselves therefore to God. Resist the devil and he will flee from you. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JAS.4.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JAS.4.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JAS 4:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Draw near to God and he will draw near to you. Cleanse your hands, you sinners, and purify your hearts, you men of double mind. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JAS.4.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JAS.4.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JAS 4:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Be wretched and mourn and weep. Let your laughter be turned to mourning and your joy to dejection. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JAS.4.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JAS.4.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JAS 4:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Humble yourselves before the Lord and he will exalt you.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JAS.4.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JAS.4.10"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JAS 4:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JAS.4.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JAS.4.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JAS 4:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Do not speak evil against one another, brethren. He that speaks evil against a brother or judges his brother, speaks evil against the law and judges the law. But if you judge the law, you are not a doer of the law but a judge. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JAS.4.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JAS.4.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JAS 4:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "There is one lawgiver and judge, he who is able to save and to destroy. But who are you that you judge your neighbor?",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JAS.4.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JAS.4.12"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JAS 4:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JAS.4.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JAS.4.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JAS 4:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Come now, you who say, “Today or tomorrow we will go into such and such a town and spend a year there and trade and get gain”; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JAS.4.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JAS.4.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JAS 4:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "whereas you do not know about tomorrow. What is your life? For you are a mist that appears for a little time and then vanishes. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JAS.4.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JAS.4.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JAS 4:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Instead you ought to say, “If the Lord wills, we shall live and we shall do this or that.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JAS.4.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JAS.4.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JAS 4:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "As it is, you boast in your arrogance. All such boasting is evil. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JAS.4.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JAS.4.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JAS 4:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Whoever knows what is right to do and fails to do it, for him it is sin.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JAS.4.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JAS.4.17"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
